
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This directory contains the pointing, efficiency function, observer ephemeris
and detections of the N26 HST heliostack: the Napier et al. (2026, Planet.
Sci. J. 7, 117; arXiv:2604.16731) reanalysis of the Bernstein et al. (2004,
AJ 128, 1364) HST GO-9433 ACS/WFC F606W field as a single 15-day heliostack.
It is a single-epoch survey (one stack), not a multi-epoch AND.

Photometry is HST ACS F606W in STMAG, filter letter t (not r, not w):

    t = STMAG_F606W = r_AB + 0.3

so colour.toml has "t-g" = "r-g" + 0.3 in every spectral group. The 0.3 mag
ST->AB conversion is the one adopted for this survey; the Napier vs Bernstein
zeropoint offset on the two objects in both catalogs is ~0.2 mag.

The content of this directory is:

N26
   \---------- README.n26 (this file)   Describes the content of the directory
    \--------- pointings.list           One rectangle: the 6-tile 400" x 600"
     \                                  ACS/WFC mosaic at 14:07:53.33
      \                                 -11:21:38, JD 2452672.8585 (stack
       \                                midpoint), fill factor 1
        \----- N26.eff                  Detection efficiency, filter= t
         \---- HST.csv                  JPL Horizons barycentric ICRF vectors
          \                             of HST (-48), 2003-Feb-02 06:00-14:00
           \                            TDB at 1 minute steps
            \- HST.jpl_batch            The Horizons batch request that
                                        produced HST.csv
   \---------- N26.csv                  The four detected objects (CSV)
    \--------- N26.toml                 survey_debias configuration

Where the values come from:

- Efficiency (N26.eff): Napier Eq. 20 logistic
      eta = eta0 / (1 + exp((m - m50)/sigma)),
      eta0 = 1.0, m50 = 29.21 +/- 0.03 STMAG, sigma = 0.11 +/- 0.02,
  written as the OSSSSim single tanh A/2 (1 - tanh((m - M0)/w)) with
  A = eta0, M0 = m50 = 29.21, w = 2 sigma = 0.22. The tracking fraction is 1
  (the characterized sample is the stack itself) with the same knee.
- mag_lim = 29.80: Napier's implant faint limit is 29.7 STMAG (Sec. III.1);
  0.1 mag of headroom keeps mag_lim off the efficiency knee.
- mag_error: the OSSOS photometric-scatter template shifted so the knee is
  at 29.2 STMAG. It is not fitted to the HST photometry.
- rate_cut = 0.05-6.4 "/hr, isotropic: the cone of the OSSSSim HST example
  (examples/Surveys/HST/HST.eff). Napier searches barycentric CCKBO
  trajectories and corrects HST parallax in the stack; this cut is the
  on-sky rate at the 15-day midpoint, not the LEO parallax loops.
- Pointing: field centre and mosaic size of the Bernstein et al. 2004
  GO-9433 field; the epoch is the 15-day stack midpoint.
- Detections (N26.csv): name, m_stmag, a, e, i, d_bary, ifree from Napier
  Tables 1 and 2. a and e are a_min and e_min. 2003 BF91 and 2003 BH91 are
  the Bernstein et al. objects; 2003 ABCD and 2003 WXYZ are new in Napier.
  FV53 and BG91 were visible in single exposures and were not part of this
  search, so they are not in the characterized sample.

These files were moved here from hst-tno-followup/characterization/ and
hst-tno-followup/data/n26_detections.csv. The .eff file there was in r_AB
(filter= r, every magnitude 0.3 brighter than here); it is now in native
STMAG so it matches the m_stmag detections.

See CFEPS_g/README.formats for the format of a survey "block".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
